\subsection{Model Train}

To train the 2D-CNN baseline model, stratified 5-fold cross-validation was used on the training data. At each step, 80\% and 20\% of the data are randomly selected as training and validation sets, respectively. Each input is used once as validation. There is the same proportion of benign/malicious examples in each cross-validation. As well as \cite{b1}, the batch size value is 64, and 30 epochs are used to train the model. At the end of the training, five models are obtained and evaluated using the test set, $D_{driving}$.

