For comparison, we followed the continual learning approach that utilizes stochastic weight averaging~\cite{izmailov2018averaging} and distillation~\cite{buzzega2020dark} (also known as Dark Experience Replay) to maintain the stability of the training course, referred as the \textbf{SWADT} model. To the best of our knowledge, this is a scalable approach applicable to end-to-end speech recognition and was demonstrated to outperform even rehearsal-based techniques. 

% In this approach, the loss function is added with the KL-divergence between the current and base models' output distributions. Furthermore, after each gradient descent update, the model weights are averaged with the pre-updated weights, with the coefficient decreasing over time. The end result is a temporal of model ensembling mitigating catastrophic forgetting, referred to as the \textbf{SWADT} model.

