% jon: tried to clarify the point. The classical 'black box codec' approach historically has led to viewers showing wrongly oriented images, misinterpreting colors, not handling grayscale or alpha correctly, etc etc.
Knowing the colorimetric interpretation of the sample data also allows a lossy encoder to make better decisions and to produce more consistent results for a given quality setting.

The remaining metadata, e.g. Exif or XMP, can be stored in the container format, but it does not influence the main image rendering (although it could describe alternative rendering options).
