% Large language models (LLMs) demonstrate strong capabilities in contextual learning, making them powerful probabilistic models for lossless data compression when paired with arithmetic coding. However, these methods' excessive computational costs limit their practical use. Besides, existing approaches tend to focus on single-modal data and lack processing flexibility. To overcome these challenges, we propose \textbf{DualComp}, a unified and lightweight framework for dual-modal lossless compression. 
