\subsection{Fundamentals of Programming Course}

Fundamentals of Programming (FoP) is an introductory, hands-on course for first-semester students in the Bachelor's program. No prior programming knowledge is required. The curriculum covers essential topics such as control structures, data types, Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) concepts, streams, graphical user interfaces (GUIs), and recursion. 
Its assessment is fully based on practical activities. As shown in Table~\ref{tab:grades}, 60\% of the final grade comes from developing and presenting a final project.

