After analyzing the results of the FoP final survey, Figure~\ref{Boxplot-Survey} shows that the experimental group reported consistently higher median scores and less variability across all three survey dimensions: communication among team members, task distribution, and communication with the tutor. In contrast, the control group responses were more dispersed, with several low outliers—particularly in team communication and tutor interaction—indicating a more uneven experience. These visual trends suggest a positive influence of the soft skills seminar on team dynamics and communication. 

