\subsection{Frequency Spectra}
%===============================================================================

In Fig.~\ref{fig:teaser} we see a comparison between frequency spectra of corresponding pairs of dimensions between SZ and Sobol sequences.
Our construction evidently admits better pairwise projections at powers of $2^q$ octaves, though the discrepancy plots in Fig.~\ref{fig:discrepancy} suggest that Sobol behaves better at a more granular powers-of-2 octaves.
Further, the fact that all consecutive pairs of dimensions of ensembled SZ sequences are dyadic $(0, 2)$-sequences makes them ripe for different optimizations of such sequences like those suggested by Ahmed et al.~\shortcite{Ahmed23DigitalSequences, Ahmed2024SobolFast} or Doignies et. al. \shortcite{Doignies2025Differentiable}.
In the supplementary materials we provide more detailed spectral plots, as well as a tool to produce more.

