\begin{assumption}\label{ass:peristency}
The input $u(t)$ used to build the training data is persistently exciting such that, for some positive $c$,
\begin{align*}
    U_{[1,\rho+\tau-1]} U_{[1,\rho+\tau-1]}^T \geq cI_{\rho+\tau-1} \: \forall \: N, % \frac{1}{N}
\end{align*}
and the variance of the noise $e(t)$ is positive definite.
\end{assumption}
Assumption \ref{ass:peristency} guarantees that that $Z_{[1,l]} Z_{[1,l]}^T$ does not become singular as $N \rightarrow \infty$ for any $l \in [\rho, \rho+\tau-1]$ and thus, given sufficient data, the single-step predictors can be estimated with arbitrary precision using \eqref{eqn:singleStepPred}.
