% Unlike SPC, in DeePC and $\gamma$-DDPC there is no closed-form mapping from $v \rightarrow y_f$. Instead, the control cost and the modeling accuracy are both present in the data-driven optimization \eqref{eqn:optiDef_gammaDDPC}, \eqref{eqn:optiDef_DeePC} \cite{dorfler2022bridging}. In DeePC \cite{coulson2019data}, the trade-off between control cost and modeling accuracy manifests as a $g$ regularization weight. In $\gamma$-DDPC, which takes the LQ decomposition of the Hankel data, the trade-off manifests as a weight on $\gamma$ regularization. %As noted in Remark \ref{rem:ddpcAndSPC}, SPC is a particular case of DeePC or $\gamma$-DDPC.

In this section we present an expression for the bias of the prediction implicit in $\gamma$-DDPC (DeePC) for a particular choice of $\gamma := \begin{bmatrix} \gamma_v^T & \gamma_{\epsilon}^T \end{bmatrix}^T$ ($g$).
First, we note that the Subspace Predictor is embedded in the LQ decomposition: %\eqref{eqn:LQdecompData}:
\begin{align*}
    \mathbb{E}\left[L_{Y V}\right] \mathbb{E}\left[L_{VV}\right]^{-1} = \mathbb{E}\left[Y_f V^T\right] \mathbb{E}\left[V V^T\right]^{-1} = S.
\end{align*}
