\section{Conclusion}

This paper quantified the Subspace Bias and the Optimism Bias of subspace-based DDPC methods and demonstrated that they impact control performance.
It also demonstrated that Transient Predictive Control, which does not suffer from Subspace Bias or Optimism Bias and is consistent regardless of how the training data are gathered, performs well with both open and closed-loop data. 


